WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.929
This chapter asks a specific question: The stack needs durable artifacts

2
00:00:04.929 --> 00:00:09.355
and replayable traces so work can be inspected, reused, tested,

3
00:00:09.355 --> 00:00:10.240
and improved.

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.389
The tempting shortcut is insufficient: If outputs are not tied to

5
00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:20.198
inputs, tools, context, claims, and logs, later verification and improvement cannot

6
00:00:20.198 --> 00:00:21.510
know what happened.

7
00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.627
The chapter's core claim is this: Execution should produce an artifact

8
00:00:26.627 --> 00:00:31.144
graph with audit logs, provenance, replay metadata, and links to claims

9
00:00:31.144 --> 00:00:31.965
and tests.

10
00:00:32.305 --> 00:00:37.866
Freeze an artifact admission envelope with stable artifact and revision identity,

11
00:00:37.866 --> 00:00:43.427
type, role, producer, parent job and attempt, intended consumers, consequence, authority,

12
00:00:43.427 --> 00:00:46.460
rights, retention, and expiry before reuse.

13
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.387
Compute content digests and, where policy matters, compound content-and-policy identities while

14
00:00:52.387 --> 00:00:57.973
treating paths, URLs, object keys, cache slots, and display names as

15
00:00:57.973 --> 00:01:00.005
mutable locations or projections.

16
00:01:00.345 --> 00:01:06.173
Bind each artifact revision to exact source, dataset, contract, plan, job,

17
00:01:06.173 --> 00:01:12.002
attempt, context transaction, semantic certificate, model, prompt, tool, adapter, code, environment,

18
00:01:12.002 --> 00:01:17.300
policy, approval, permission, cost, and residual lineage that actually applied.

19
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.930
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

20
00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:27.286
The current minimum is two public artifact/projection schemas;

21
00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:33.555
2 valid/6 rejecting replay fixtures; 1 valid/10 rejecting projection-revocation records;

22
00:01:33.555 --> 00:01:39.825
1 valid/4 rejecting record-reality sequences; 3 valid/6 rejecting receipt-faithfulness records;

23
00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:45.421
a four-surface repository audit with 55 digest checks and five mutations;

24
00:01:45.421 --> 00:01:50.677
four deterministic challenges and five mutations; one live artifact with three

25
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:55.934
observation routes and seven mutations; four sampled artifacts with twelve observation

26
00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.845
routes and eight mutations;

27
00:01:58.185 --> 00:02:04.188
3 valid/6 rejecting epistemic-TCB records; one historical GitHub Actions service record;

28
00:02:04.188 --> 00:02:09.099
one historical public-page fetch record; eight accepted no-promotion decisions;

29
00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:13.465
and forty-three Lean declarations under ten public targets.

30
00:02:14.065 --> 00:02:19.115
The design can still fail. Artifact amnesia leaves useful or harmful

31
00:02:19.115 --> 00:02:24.165
work products without stable identity, parent work, source, context, tool, effect,

32
00:02:24.165 --> 00:02:26.920
claim, test, owner, or residual lineage.

33
00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.324
Path and name authority makes relocation, cache movement, renaming,

34
00:02:31.324 --> 00:02:36.290
or object-store migration change identity or silently bind the wrong bytes.

35
00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:42.264
Provenance theater records plausible asserted edges while actual inputs, transformations,

36
00:02:42.264 --> 00:02:47.335
side effects, omitted dependencies, or responsible actors remain unknown.

37
00:02:47.675 --> 00:02:52.241
Audit-log theater accepts mutable, dropped, selectively written, unauthenticated, inaccessible,

38
00:02:52.241 --> 00:02:57.821
or producer-controlled events as a complete reconstruction. The correct response is

39
00:02:57.821 --> 00:03:03.401
to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate, or retain an owned residual rather

40
00:03:03.401 --> 00:03:05.430
than narrate uncertainty away.

41
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:11.076
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

42
00:03:11.076 --> 00:03:15.205
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

43
00:03:15.205 --> 00:03:20.251
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

44
00:03:20.251 --> 00:03:20.710
closed.

45
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:27.377
A reachable artifact lifecycle preserves exact artifact, content, parent-job, source, context,

46
00:03:27.377 --> 00:03:33.704
transaction, certificate, tool, claim, test, policy, and consumer custody from registration

47
00:03:33.704 --> 00:03:38.880
through consumer-acknowledged admission without assigning support or external effects.

48
00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:47.259
Missing provenance, replay, observation, cross-check, trap, attestation-limit, trust-root, verifier-separation, recursion-stop, residual,

49
00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:52.375
revocation, or consumer obligations block lifecycle progress.

50
00:03:52.975 --> 00:03:57.939
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

51
00:03:57.939 --> 00:04:02.903
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

52
00:04:02.903 --> 00:04:07.867
deployment. A local check or formal model does not establish real-world

53
00:04:07.867 --> 00:04:12.380
enforcement. No safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI, or ASI conclusion follows.

54
00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.195
These boundaries matter because an explanatory derivative is useful only if

55
00:04:17.195 --> 00:04:20.450
it preserves the evidence ceiling of its source.

56
00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:26.206
At most, this visual explains the chapter's design rationale at argument

57
00:04:26.206 --> 00:04:30.893
support; it adds no empirical, deployment, safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI,

58
00:04:30.893 --> 00:04:36.049
or ASI result. The next chapter is Runtime Adapters, Tool Permissions,

59
00:04:36.049 --> 00:04:37.455
and Human Approval.

60
00:04:37.795 --> 00:04:42.794
It takes responsibility for Plans become real-world effects only through tools,

61
00:04:42.794 --> 00:04:47.792
runtimes, deployment adapters, and approval gates. Read the live chapter for

62
00:04:47.792 --> 00:04:51.882
its complete source mappings, interfaces, invariants, failure modes, tests,

63
00:04:51.882 --> 00:04:53.700
and open evidence gaps.
